## Device details

### HP EliteDesk (Proxmox server)

| Item | Details |
|---|---|
| Model | HP EliteDesk mini PC (exact model _unknown_) |
| CPU | Intel Core i5 |
| RAM | 16 GB |
| Storage | _unknown_ |
| Network | 1 Gb Ethernet |
| Role | Proxmox VE host |

Notes:

- A TrueNAS VM can use most of the 16 GB. Give it a fixed amount (for example 6 to 8 GB) and leave the rest for the host and containers.
- Containers use far less memory than VMs. Vaultwarden, NPM and Pi-hole each need very little.
- Mini PCs usually take two SO-DIMM sticks, so check the model's maximum before upgrading RAM.
- A small UPS protects against power cuts, which can corrupt VMs and storage.

